import{c as t,Q as o,j as a,m as s}from"./chunks/framework.BXc4yaFE.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"Self-Evolving Autoresearch Workflow Loops","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"research/tweets/2026-06-09-@alokbishoyi97-525741.md","filePath":"research/tweets/2026-06-09-@alokbishoyi97-525741.md","lastUpdated":1785909234000}'),r={name:"research/tweets/2026-06-09-@alokbishoyi97-525741.md"};function n(i,e,h,l,d,p){return o(),a("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[s('<h1 id="self-evolving-autoresearch-workflow-loops" tabindex="-1">Self-Evolving Autoresearch Workflow Loops <a class="header-anchor" href="#self-evolving-autoresearch-workflow-loops" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Self-Evolving Autoresearch Workflow Loops&quot;">​</a></h1><p><strong>作者</strong>：Alok Bishoyi (@alokbishoyi97)<br><strong>發布時間</strong>：2026-06-09<br><strong>原始連結</strong>：<a href="https://x.com/alokbishoyi97/status/2064281952631525741" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://x.com/alokbishoyi97/status/2064281952631525741</a><br><strong>類型</strong>：Twitter Article<br><strong>統計</strong>：❤️ 315 · 🔁 45 · 🔖 542 · 👁 25,428</p><hr><h2 id="分析摘要" tabindex="-1">分析摘要 <a class="header-anchor" href="#分析摘要" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;分析摘要&quot;">​</a></h2><p><strong>TL;DR</strong>：evo autoresearch orchestrator 將 loop 遷移到 dynamic workflows，並進一步實現自我演化（meta loop 在 optimize loop 運行時重寫 optimize loop 的 harness）。雙 async loop 架構：<code>Promise.all</code> 並行 optimize + meta；meta 每隔幾分鐘讀取整個 run 並 emit harness edits / brief hints / stops / alerts。</p><h3 id="核心論點" tabindex="-1">核心論點 <a class="header-anchor" href="#核心論點" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;核心論點&quot;">​</a></h3><ol><li><strong>從 in-context orchestration 到 workflow 的動機</strong>：長 run 中 prompt/instruction adherence 不可靠——phases、CLI commands、去重規則在 context 延長後「悄悄停止發生」；loop 遷移到 workflow 讓 method 成為 code，phases/stopping rule/gates/CLI calls 是 script 的一部分，round 1 和 round 1000 行為相同</li><li><strong>evo optimize loop 六步</strong>：orient（讀 experiment tree）→ scan（parallel agents 找 pattern）→ ideate（stall 時三個 research agents：最佳分支推演 + 失敗分析 + 文獻研究）→ brief（去重 experiment briefs）→ fan-out（parallel 實作+pre-verify+audit）→ collect（剪枝、記錄）</li><li><strong>自我演化架構（最核心創新）</strong>：meta loop 與 optimize loop 同一 event loop 運行（<code>Promise.all</code>），共享一個 harness 物件；optimize loop 每 round 讀 harness，meta 每隔幾分鐘寫 harness；meta 可：注入/移除 steps、rewrite phases、添加 verifier、調整 width/stall 參數</li><li><strong>四種 meta output</strong>：harness edits（最強）/ brief hints（軟性，入下一輪 brief）/ stops（交 gated enforcer，detect 和 act 分離，禁 silent kill）/ alerts（人工介入）</li><li><strong>關鍵設計原則</strong>：harness edits 交由 meta，stops 交由 gated enforcer（而非 meta 直接 kill）；外部觀察者在課業修正和捕捉問題上非常有效</li></ol><h3 id="關鍵設計洞察" tabindex="-1">關鍵設計洞察 <a class="header-anchor" href="#關鍵設計洞察" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;關鍵設計洞察&quot;">​</a></h3><blockquote><p>&quot;The loop&#39;s shape becomes data the system changes to match what the run actually needs.&quot;</p></blockquote><p>「Loop 的形狀本身成為資料，系統在運行中改變它以適應需求」——這是 meta-programming of agent loops 的核心思想。</p><h3 id="批判性觀察" tabindex="-1">批判性觀察 <a class="header-anchor" href="#批判性觀察" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;批判性觀察&quot;">​</a></h3><ol><li>evo 是 open source（github.com/evo-hq/evo），有可驗證的實作，可信度高</li><li><code>Promise.all</code> 共享 harness object 的線程安全假設（寫在 optimizer awaits 之間）值得關注</li><li>成本/效果量化數據未提供——自我演化是否比固定 loop 顯著提升需更多證據</li><li>&quot;detect and act stay separate; never a silent kill&quot; 是安全設計的好原則</li></ol><hr><h2 id="評分" tabindex="-1">評分 <a class="header-anchor" href="#評分" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;評分&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>維度</th><th>分數</th><th>理由</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>A. Workspace 可行動性</td><td>6/10</td><td>evo CLI 特定；但雙 async loop + shared harness object 模式可移植到 cc-workspace</td></tr><tr><td>B. 創新性</td><td>9/10</td><td>Meta loop 在 optimize loop 運行中 rewrite harness 是目前最前沿的自我演化設計；loop shape as data 是全新框架</td></tr><tr><td>C. 證據品質</td><td>7/10</td><td>Open source 實作（可驗證）；evo-optimize.js 可直接讀；無量化性能數據</td></tr><tr><td>D. 技術深度</td><td>8/10</td><td>雙 async loop、harness 物件共享、四種 meta output 分類、stops 的 gated enforcer 設計細節紮實</td></tr><tr><td>E. 泛化性</td><td>7/10</td><td>自我演化 meta loop 模式可泛化到任何長 horizon iterative optimization 系統</td></tr><tr><td><strong>加權總分</strong></td><td><strong>7.25/10</strong></td><td>A×0.3 + B×0.2 + C×0.2 + D×0.15 + E×0.15</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>整合決策</strong>：Rule<br><strong>整合位置</strong>：<code>subagent-strategy.md</code>：meta-loop pattern（外部觀察者 + harness 物件修改）作為 dynamic workflow 進階模式；<code>refs/harness-meta-GOTCHAS.md</code>：detect-and-act 分離（stops → gated enforcer，禁 silent kill）<br><strong>整合狀態</strong>：待實作</p><hr><h2 id="全文" tabindex="-1">全文 <a class="header-anchor" href="#全文" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;全文&quot;">​</a></h2><p>In this article we explain how we ported evo&#39;s autoresearch loop to use workflows and then also made it dynamic.</p><p>On June 2 Anthropic shipped dynamic workflows in Claude Code: Claude writes a small JavaScript program on the fly that spawns and coordinates subagents. The coordination runs as code; the model does the judgment. The thing to take away is that orchestration itself moved off the model&#39;s decision and can now be described as code.</p><h2 id="what-evo-is" tabindex="-1">what evo is <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-evo-is" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;what evo is&quot;">​</a></h2><p>evo is an autoresearch orchestrator. You give it a system, a definition of &quot;better,&quot; and a budget. It generates hypotheses, runs each one in its own isolated workspace, scores it, and keeps a tree of attempts - extending what works, pruning what doesn&#39;t - while an auditor checks every accepted change so the optimizer can&#39;t game the metric. Open source; runs on Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, and others.</p><h2 id="why-we-moved-the-loop-onto-workflows" tabindex="-1">why we moved the loop onto workflows <a class="header-anchor" href="#why-we-moved-the-loop-onto-workflows" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;why we moved the loop onto workflows&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The loop used to be orchestrated in-context, as one long agent run holding the whole plan: which phase comes next, how many experiments to launch, when to stop. evo does autoresearch in an opinionated way, and at every step the agent has to follow that method and drive the CLI we ship alongside it. Over a long autoresearch run, getting the agent to adhere to all of that was tricky. Prompt and instruction adherence is unreliable on long-horizon tasks: across dozens of rounds the standing rules quietly stop happening, and the longer a single context runs, the less it holds.</p><p>Moving the loop onto a dynamic workflow fixes that at the root. The method is the code now: the phases, the fan-out width, the stopping rule, the gates, and the CLI calls are part of the script, deterministic and the same on round 1 and round 1000. Adherence stops being something the model has to remember. Every step is a fresh, scoped subagent with one job and a clean context, so there&#39;s nothing to drift. The model does judgment; the code does coordination.</p><h2 id="what-the-evo-autoresearch-workflow-runs-one-round" tabindex="-1">what the evo autoresearch workflow runs: one round <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-the-evo-autoresearch-workflow-runs-one-round" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;what the evo autoresearch workflow runs: one round&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Each round of the optimize loop walks the same six steps, in code:</p><ul><li><strong>Orient</strong>: Read the experiment tree: best score, the ceiling, the open frontier. Take the top width frontier nodes as this round&#39;s parents.</li><li><strong>Scan</strong>: Agents comb the evaluated nodes in parallel for what&#39;s working and what&#39;s failing, while an aggregate agent looks for patterns across the whole tree.</li><li><strong>Ideate</strong>: On a stall, three research agents fire at once: one extrapolates the best branch, one dissects the failures, one reads the literature and the web.</li><li><strong>Brief</strong>: A writer folds the scan findings, the patterns, and the ideas into concrete experiment briefs, then dedupes them.</li><li><strong>Fan-out</strong>: One lane per brief, in parallel. Each lane implements the change, pre-verifies it (and revises if it&#39;s gaming the metric), runs it, then post-audits with the verifier.</li><li><strong>Collect</strong>: Prune dead lineages, record notes, and repeat until the score stops improving.</li></ul><p>It worked, but the workflow still ran same shape every round: the same phases, the same steps, the same prompts, no matter what the run had learned about itself. A long run turns up things a fixed shape can&#39;t handle.</p><h2 id="now-the-loop-evolves-itself" tabindex="-1">now: the loop evolves itself <a class="header-anchor" href="#now-the-loop-evolves-itself" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;now: the loop evolves itself&quot;">​</a></h2><p>evo 0.5 makes the optimize loop self-evolving. A second workflow runs alongside the first. Two async loops on one event loop, joined with <code>Promise.all</code>:</p><ul><li>the <strong>optimize loop</strong> is the driver, the above defined workflow, unchanged</li><li>the <strong>meta loop</strong> is a concurrent observer: a fresh agent that wakes every few minutes, reads the run from the outside, and rewrites the optimize loop while it runs</li></ul><p>They share one plain object, the harness: the steps the loop runs, the phases and the prompts they use, the gates and verifiers in play (alongside knobs like width and stall that were always adjustable). The optimizer reads it every round; the meta thread writes it. Same event loop, so writes land between the optimizer&#39;s awaits, with no locks and no second process.</p><h2 id="what-the-meta-can-do" tabindex="-1">what the meta can do <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-the-meta-can-do" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;what the meta can do&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Each tick it observes the tree, the scores, the live logs, GPU and host state (strictly read-only), and emits four kinds of output:</p><ul><li><strong>harness edits</strong>: the real lever. A run surfaces needs specific to it: this experiment class wants its own verifier step, that one needs a particular method injected, another step turns out to be dead weight and should be cut. The meta adapts the workflow to fit, injecting steps, removing them, and rewriting the phases that run. It takes effect on the next round. The loop&#39;s shape becomes data the system changes to match what the run actually needs.</li><li><strong>brief hints</strong>: softer; queued into the next round&#39;s brief to nudge what it tries next.</li><li><strong>stops</strong>: when an experiment is going nowhere the meta doesn&#39;t kill it. It hands a recommendation to a separate gated enforcer that verifies, aborts, diagnoses, and discards. Detect and act stay separate; never a silent kill.</li><li><strong>alerts</strong>: runtime problems it can&#39;t fix itself (e.g. a dying GPU) go to a human.</li></ul><p>We have found that having an external observer / meta agent look at the experiments and nudge it to be very effective in course correcting and catching issues.</p><h2 id="takeaways" tabindex="-1">Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Dynamic workflows make coordination code instead of context. What that buys you is that the loop becomes a first-class object, something you can read, edit, and reason about while it runs, instead of a harness you write once and hope fits every round. The loop&#39;s own shape is one more parameter space that can be evolved.</p><p>evo is open source. You can go through the dynamic workflow implementation at <a href="https://github.com/evo-hq/evo/blob/main/plugins/evo/skills/optimize/workflows/evo-optimize.js" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://github.com/evo-hq/evo/blob/main/plugins/evo/skills/optimize/workflows/evo-optimize.js</a></p>',40)])])}const m=t(r,[["render",n]]);export{u as __pageData,m as default};
